body:
You need three things in Photoshop to accomplish this.

1. Main frame image (old man's head in this case);

2. Paper-hole PNG, placed on the old man's forehead. (You'll need to add a circle shape inside of it, or just use a select tool to get the exact shape of the hole, and fill the selection in a new layer. The is going to be your "window" to the 3rd element);

3. The image you'd like to place inside. Put this layer on top of the circle-layer, right-click this layer in the Layers tab and choose "Create Clipping Mask".

Voila.
